<p class="isSelectedEnd"><strong>How to choose an interior design style</strong> becomes much easier when you stop trying to give your home a label and start thinking about how you want it to feel. When embarking on <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/residential-interior-design-london/">luxury residential interior design in London</a>, contemporary, traditional, minimalist, industrial and eclectic styles can all look beautiful, but the right choice depends on your property, lifestyle and personal taste.</p>

<h2>What Feeling Do You Want Your Interior to Create?</h2>
<p class="isSelectedEnd">Before saving hundreds of images on Pinterest, ask yourself a simpler question: <strong>How do I want to feel when I walk into this room?</strong></p>
<p class="isSelectedEnd">Do you want calm and relaxed? Warm and welcoming? Dramatic and sophisticated? Bright and energetic?</p>
<p class="isSelectedEnd">Your answer can help narrow down the colours, materials, furniture and lighting that will suit you.</p>

<h2>How Should Your Home's Architecture Influence Your Style?</h2>
<img class="alignnone wp-image-11229 size-full" src="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Start-With-the-Architecture-Not-the-Accessories.webp" alt="" width="1408" height="768" />
<p class="isSelectedEnd">Your property's existing character should influence your design choices.</p>
<p class="isSelectedEnd">A Victorian terrace may look particularly striking when original fireplaces, cornicing or timber floors are retained alongside contemporary furniture. A modern apartment might naturally lend itself to cleaner lines and simpler detailing, where integrating <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/interior-architecture/">prime London interior architecture</a> helps unlock structural light and proportion.</p>
<p class="isSelectedEnd">You don't have to choose between old and new. Some of the most interesting interiors come from combining them.</p>

<h3>How Should Your Lifestyle Affect Your Interior Design Choices?</h3>
<p class="isSelectedEnd">A style may look fantastic in a photograph but be completely wrong for your lifestyle.</p>
<p class="isSelectedEnd">If you have children, pets or frequently entertain guests, an extremely delicate interior may become impractical. If you work from home, your design needs to accommodate comfortable and functional working areas.</p>
<p class="isSelectedEnd">Think about the rooms you use most and what you need from them before choosing a particular aesthetic. A professional <strong><a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/luxury-interior-designers-in-london/">interior design company</a></strong> can also help you balance style, comfort and everyday practicality.</p>

<h3>Do All the Furniture and Accessories Need to Match?</h3>
[caption id="attachment_4509" align="alignnone" width="1200"]<img class="wp-image-4509 size-full" src="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/Bespoke-Furniture-London-Custom-Pieces-That-Transform-Your-Home.jpeg" alt="A luxurious London living room featuring a bespoke blue velvet curved sofa with a brass base, a custom marble and wood block coffee table, a handcrafted fluted media console, and built-in illuminated cabinetry." width="1200" height="655" /> This elegant London living space showcases the transformative power of bespoke furniture, from the statement curved sofa to the unique, custom-designed coffee table and cabinetry, creating a truly one-of-a-kind home.[/caption]
<p class="isSelectedEnd">Choosing one style doesn't mean every piece of furniture needs to look as though it came from the same collection.</p>
<p class="isSelectedEnd">Mixing materials, periods and textures can make an interior feel much more personal. For inspiration on blending current styling cues, explore our guide on <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/contemporary-home-decorating-ideas/">contemporary home decorating ideas</a>.</p>
<p class="isSelectedEnd">For example, incorporating <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/bespoke-furniture-london-custom-pieces-that-transform-your-home/">bespoke furniture in London</a> can work beautifully with traditional architectural details, while natural timber can soften a minimalist scheme.</p>
<p class="isSelectedEnd">The goal is <strong>cohesion, not uniformity</strong>.</p>

<h3>How Can You Create a Colour Palette for Your Home?</h3>
<p class="isSelectedEnd">Colour is often where people become overwhelmed.</p>
<p class="isSelectedEnd">Instead of choosing a different colour for every room, start with a few tones that you genuinely like. These can then be adapted throughout the house.</p>
<p class="isSelectedEnd">Consider how your chosen colours work with your home's architecture, natural light, flooring and furniture. A consistent palette can help different rooms feel connected without making them identical, creating cohesion across your living spaces much like our curated <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/sitting-room-interior-design-ideas-stylish-comfortable-modern-ways-to-transform-your-space/">sitting room interior design ideas</a>.</p>

<h3>Why Is Lighting Important When Choosing an Interior Design Style?</h3>
[caption id="attachment_8760" align="alignnone" width="672"]<img class="wp-image-8760 size-full" src="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/01/Modern-Small-Lounge-Design-with-Sectional-Sofa-and-Marble-Coffee-Table.jpg" alt="Modern small lounge interior with grey sectional sofa, marble coffee table, and recessed ceiling lighting" width="672" height="372" /> Sleek modern lounge design with soft neutrals, ambient lighting, and a minimalist seating layout.[/caption]
<p class="isSelectedEnd">The same room can feel completely different under different lighting.</p>
<p class="isSelectedEnd">Natural daylight, pendant lights, wall lights, floor lamps and accent lighting all contribute to the atmosphere.</p>
<p class="isSelectedEnd">This is why lighting should be considered alongside your chosen style rather than added at the end.</p>
<p class="isSelectedEnd">A warm, traditional interior may benefit from soft layered lighting, while a contemporary space might use architectural lighting to emphasise clean lines and materials.</p>

<h3>What Should You Do If You Like More Than One Interior Design Style?</h3>
